 "management": "Dr. Mehra-Castillo graduated from veterinary school in 2006 and worked eight years at a 24-hour emergency hospital before joining Cottonwood Creek as an associate in 2014; she bought the practice from the founder in 2019. Practice manager Rosalind Teague (since 2016) handles payroll, inventory and the wellness-plan billing; she holds a certified practice manager credential. The three associates have been with the practice an average of 5.5 years. The owner works clinical shifts four days a week and keeps one day for management. Succession: the practice carries $2,000,000 of key-person life insurance on the owner, assignable to the bank, and a disability buy-out policy.",
 "site_visit": "Analyst and SBA loan officer Miguel Ostrander toured the hospital on 2026-09-17 during a Thursday afternoon clinic. Waiting room was full (nine clients with pets at 3:40 p.m.). The existing surgery room handles roughly 14 procedures a day and is booked about three weeks out for non-urgent dentals. The proposed second suite will occupy what is now a storage area and part of the staff break room; the contractor's bid (Ridgeway Builders, $238,500 plus a 5% contingency) is in the file. The isolation ward is required by the practice's updated infection-control protocol after a parvovirus cluster in the county in 2025. Parking: 31 spaces, shared access drive with a dental office next door, which has a recorded easement. Signage is visible from the state highway.",
 "projections_summary": "Management projects 2027 revenue of $4.32 million (+9.3%), driven by the surgical suite (about $310,000 in year one, assuming the boarded surgeon starts by March 2027) and 4% fee increases. The analyst's sensitivity case assumes no surgical revenue at all and flat fees: 2027 cash flow available for debt service would then be roughly $640,000, still above the projected business debt service. Wellness-plan revenue is recurring monthly and was $588,000 in 2025.",
 "insurance_and_licensing": "State veterinary premises permit current through 2027-06-30; DEA registration current; all four veterinarians hold active state licenses with no disciplinary history on the state board's public lookup. Property and liability insurance with Prairie Mutual; the bank will be added as mortgagee and lender loss payee. Professional liability coverage $1,000,000 per occurrence.",
 "appraisal_summary": "Plains Valuation Group relied mainly on the sales comparison approach (four sales of medical and veterinary buildings within 35 miles, adjusted for age and lot size) and cross-checked with the income approach using a market rent of $17.50 per square foot and a 7.75% capitalization rate. The appraiser notes that special-purpose features (kennel runs, drains, lead-lined X-ray room) add little value for non-veterinary buyers, so a forced sale to another type of user could take longer. Remaining economic life is estimated at 30 years. No deferred maintenance beyond resealing the parking lot (about $9,000).",
